/packs/
/.vscode/
/.claude/
# The six top-level spec/decision documents are PUBLISHED (2026-08-16): they are
# the format contract CLAUDE.md, backend/CLAUDE.md and delta_test.go cite as
# mandatory pre-reading, so a public clone must carry them. Everything else under
# /docs/ — findings, superpowers plans/specs — stays local-only working material
# (see CLAUDE.md's store-visibility reasoning for why internal planning does not
# get published).
/docs/*
!/docs/MANIFEST-SPEC.md
!/docs/MULTI-STORE-SPEC.md
!/docs/DELTA-TAIL-SPEC.md
!/docs/INBOX-SPEC.md
!/docs/STORE-VISIBILITY.md
!/docs/STATIC-ENGINE-DECISION.md
/FINDINGS-PLAN.md
/.wrangler/

# Frontend
/frontend/node_modules/
/frontend/.parcel-cache/
/frontend/dist/
/dist/

# The admin console is a Parcel bundle built into backend/webui/dist by
# `make build-admin` — generated, like /dist. The tracked .gitkeep is what lets
# a Node-less `go build`/`go vet`/`go test` compile the //go:embed (the `all:`
# prefix embeds dotfiles); no build ever writes that name, so nothing here can
# turn up dirty. Serve answers "/" from unbuiltNote when index.html is absent.
/backend/webui/dist/*
!/backend/webui/dist/.gitkeep

# design-sync build output (regenerable; see .design-sync/NOTES.md)
/ds-bundle/

# SRR Cloud worker (cloud/worker): the staged shell bundle is generated by
# `make build-cloud` from dist/srrf; wrangler state, the real dev secrets and
# the real deployment config never belong in git — this repo is public, and
# wrangler.toml carries one operator's hostname, zone and login URL while
# .dev.vars carries the session secret and the tenant roster (personal data).
# Both have committed templates: wrangler.example.toml and .dev.vars.example,
# and `make` materializes wrangler.toml from its example when absent.
#
# public-reader/ is the same generated bundle for the hosted reader Worker
# (`make build-reader`, absolute cdn-url). Its wrangler.reader.toml IS tracked,
# unlike the one above: it deliberately names no route, so it carries nothing
# about where this is deployed — CI supplies the hostname at deploy time.
/cloud/worker/public/
/cloud/worker/public-reader/
/cloud/worker/node_modules/
/cloud/worker/.wrangler/
/cloud/worker/.dev.vars
/cloud/worker/wrangler.toml
.worktrees/
.superpowers/
